      "level": 2,
      "content": "2.1 Physical Geography"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Gujarat's terrain is broadly divided into Mainland Gujarat, Saurashtra peninsula, and the Rann of Kutch.",
        "Important west-flowing river systems include the Narmada, Tapi, Mahi, and Sabarmati.",
        "The Rann of Kutch is a unique geographical feature comprising seasonal salt marshes divided into Great and Little Rann.",
        "The state's administrative setup comprises 33 districts spanning diverse climatic and physical landscapes."
      ],
      "id": "6vpgrv9"
